Round tax per line instead of once on the subtotal

Finance reconciles each printed invoice line against the ERP export,
which stores tax per line. Rounding once on the subtotal made the sum of
the per-line tax in the ERP differ from our printed tax by up to a cent
per line, and every mismatch opened a manual reconciliation. Tax is now
computed and rounded on each line, and the invoice tax is the sum of the
lines. See INV-7.
